Subject: Include <signal.h> before gzip.h to avoid head macro clash
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: gzip.h defines a macro named head that collides with struct members in Linux kernel sigcontext headers pulled in by <signal.h>.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: cede3de0

diff --git a/gzip.c b/gzip.c
--- a/gzip.c
+++ b/gzip.c
@@ -57,6 +57,10 @@
 #include <config.h>
 
 #include "tailor.h"
+
+/* Include <signal.h> before gzip.h so the head macro does not clash
+   with kernel sigcontext struct fields. */
+#include <signal.h>
 
 #include "gzip.h"
 #include "lzw.h"
